Don't rewrite POSIX paths handed to ./configure.

toUnix on POSIX split and rejoined the path, which turns /build/pkg
into //build/pkg (splitDirectories keeps the root as a component).
The configure script then sees $srcdir = //build/pkg, and nixpkgs'
cc-wrapper drops -I//build/pkg/include (it only admits include paths
under the store and $NIX_BUILD_TOP, compared as a string prefix), so
GHC's rts configure fails its deriveConstants probe on
rts/PosixSource.h.  stable-haskell/master had toUnix s = s (66bfdbf03);
the merge lost it.

diff --git a/src/Distribution/Simple/ConfigureScript.hs b/src/Distribution/Simple/ConfigureScript.hs
index cd9a01c4c..31a5460fc 100644
--- a/src/Distribution/Simple/ConfigureScript.hs
+++ b/src/Distribution/Simple/ConfigureScript.hs
@@ -258,7 +258,13 @@ toUnix s = let tmp = normalise s
                parts = FilePath.splitDirectories rest
            in  l ++ intercalate "/" parts
 #else
-toUnix s = intercalate "/" $ FilePath.splitDirectories s
+-- A POSIX path is already a Unix path. Splitting and rejoining it is not
+-- the identity: 'FilePath.splitDirectories' keeps the root as its own
+-- component, so @"/build/pkg"@ comes back as @"//build/pkg"@. That leaks
+-- into the script's @$srcdir@ and every @-I$srcdir/...@ it derives, and a
+-- compiler wrapper that only admits include paths under a known prefix
+-- (nixpkgs' cc-wrapper: the store and @$NIX_BUILD_TOP@) drops them.
+toUnix s = s
 #endif
 
 badAutoconfCharacters :: [(Char, String)]
